{"author":{"id":"d4d77c46d796577aec35d160aa1e09aa095720b03e93f3ca34ad3c079140e2fb"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794731232,"nonce":"FB1vYXL1NJ2tXlc1JJ1fq1eHnY0=","title":"A @const takes one value per shader class","message":"The native targets need every pipeline constant fixed, and `@:constants` gives one set of values per class, so a shader used with `fog` both on and off needs two classes. Heaps uses `@const` for exactly these variants. A list of value sets, each becoming its own set of native sources and selected at run time by its values, would cover it; russl's `#if` on pipeline constants is the same idea on its side.","files":null}]}